<title>JAPAN: Nihon Unicom Singapore starts commodity business.</title>
<headline>Nihon Unicom Singapore starts commodity business.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nihon Unicom Ltd, a commodity broker, said on Monday its Singapore subsidiary had started taking orders from Southeast Asian investors for Japanese commodity futures.</p>
<p>Nihon Unicom Singapore Pte Ltd has started taking orders for Japanese commodity futures contracts including precious metals, corn, soybeans and rubber.</p>
<p>&quot;We'll use brokers in Malaysia, Thailand and Singapore as intermediaries,&quot; a Nihon Unicom spokesman in Tokyo said.</p>
<p>Nihon Unicom Singapore is a member of the Singapore Commodity Exchange.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
